%% class: center

# Everything Carve can put on a slide

Diagrams, charts, math, real SVG, and the parts of the language a deck actually uses.

%% notes

Every slide after this one is rendered from Carve source with no raw HTML anywhere.

---

%% toc

## What is in here

---

## Mermaid, drawn on the slide

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[deck.crv] --> B{reveal-carve}
    B --> C[browser]
    B --> D[static page]
    B --> E[handout.md]
```

{.note}
:::
`--extension mermaid`. Carve emits the block, Mermaid draws the SVG.
:::

---

## A sequence, same idea

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    Author->>Carve: deck.crv
    Carve->>reveal: slide markup
    reveal->>Audience: slides
    Author->>Handout: same source
```

---

## A chart from data in the source

```chart
{
  "type": "bar",
  "data": {
    "labels": ["Markdown", "Carve"],
    "datasets": [{
      "label": "Escapes needed in the sample above",
      "data": [11, 0],
      "backgroundColor": ["#9ca3af", "#d33c43"]
    }]
  },
  "options": {
    "plugins": { "legend": { "display": false } },
    "scales": { "y": { "beginAtZero": true } }
  }
}
```

{.note}
:::
`--extension chart`. The JSON is Chart.js configuration, kept in the deck source.
:::

---

## Real SVG, inline in the source

```svg
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 240 90"
     role="img" aria-label="Three boxes">
  <rect x="4" y="20" width="66" height="44" rx="6" fill="#d33c43"/>
  <rect x="86" y="20" width="66" height="44" rx="6" fill="#6b7280"/>
  <rect x="168" y="20" width="66" height="44" rx="6" fill="#1f7a4d"/>
  <path d="M74 42h8M156 42h8" stroke="#374151" stroke-width="3"/>
</svg>
```

{.note}
:::
`--extension imgFence:{"language":"svg"}`. The SVG is sanitized and emitted as a data URI, so nothing external is loaded.
:::

---

## Math

```math
t_{upgrade} = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \left( c_i \cdot d_i \right) + r
```

{.note}
:::
`--extension mathBlock` plus KaTeX on the page.
:::

---

## Footnotes and definitions

CakePHP 5 removed every deprecation that was live in 4.5[^1].

:: Deprecation
: An API that still works but is scheduled to disappear.
:: Rector
: The tool that applies the mechanical part of an upgrade.

---

## Task lists and admonitions

- [x] Tests green on 4.5
- [x] Deprecations resolved
- [ ] PHP 8.1 in production
- [ ] Plugins checked

::: warning
Run the upgrade tool *before* bumping the dependency. Afterwards it cannot resolve the old class names.
:::

---

## The small type

Press [Ctrl]{kbd} then [S]{kbd} to open the speaker view. [HTML]{abbr="HyperText Markup Language"} is rendered as an abbreviation.

Text can be =highlighted=, struck ~through~, raised to x{^2^} or lowered to H{,2,}O.

Brand red is :color[#d33c43], the muted tone is :color[#6b7280].

---

## Quotes and tables

> The slides are the handout, and that is the problem.

|= Feature |= Markdown |= Carve |
| Escaping in code | required | none |
| Columns | HTML | containers |
| Includes | none | `{{ path }}` |
| Lint | style only | structural |

---

